    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλᾰχ-όθεν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from many places</i> or
				<i>sides,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				842c
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὁμολογεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					178c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>from many considerations, for many reasons,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ξυνέβη . . ἀναχωρῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
